# Git LFS — generated mockup rasters (AGL-149 campaign).
# These are ~1.5 MB each and there are 48+; they are design evidence, not source.
#
# Prerequisite, once per machine:  brew install git-lfs && git lfs install
#
# NOTE for scripts/make-release.py: it reads bytes from the WORKING TREE
# (path.read_bytes()), not from git. On a checkout where LFS objects have been
# smudged it archives the real PNGs; on a clone where they have not, it would
# archive the 130-byte pointer files instead — silently, and the archive would
# no longer be reproducible across checkouts. Either keep these paths out of the
# archive, or make the release gate assert real PNG bytes.
design/mockups/images/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
